{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"wall_stone_cracked","model_identifier":"wall_stone_cracked","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# wall_stone_cracked\n\nDamaged state below 70 % HP of `wall_stone` (Patch 5): the same stone piece with dark cracks, a few tips or merlons knocked off and splinters or chips. The game swaps it in below 70 % HP and back above 70 % when repaired.\n\nStone wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Stone: grey blocks, 3.6 m (128 u), one merlon, a walkway on top.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..122, z -13..10 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 8, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 128 x 16 centred at x 0, z 0\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 119, 2)"},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"stone_wall#aba79d","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-8,0,-8],"to":[8,118,8],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0,0,0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[42,0,58,118],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[58,0,74,118],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[74,0,90,118],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[90,0,106,118],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[188,0,204,16],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[204,0,220,16],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"9b7a7220-01b2-590e-86c2-2267aa50d783"},{"name"